The bug was caused by the `HASH_OF_MAPS` implementation not properly releasing the inner map pointer during the `bpf_map_elem_update()` operation. This oversight occurred due to the per-cpu `extra_elems` optimization, which bypassed the `free_htab_elem()` logic that was responsible for performing the necessary cleanups, leading to a memory leak.

